er a gunshot wound</article-title><source>Surgery</source><year>1960</year><volume>48</volume><fpage>946</fpage><lpage>951</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">13784832</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Omer</surname><given-names>GE</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Gelberman RH</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Nerve injuries associated with gunshot wounds of the extremities</article-title><source>Operative Nerve Repair and Reconstruction</source><year>1991</year><volume>1</volume><publisher-name>Philadelphia: Lippincott</publisher-name><fpage>655</fpage><lpage>670</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sedel</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Terzis JK</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Surgical management of the lower extremity nerve lesions: clinical evaluation, surgical technique, results</article-title><source>Microreconstruction of Nerve Injuries</source><year>1987</year><publisher-name>Philadelphia: W.B. Saunders Co</publisher-name><fpage>253</fpage><lpage>265</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dubuisson</surname><given-names>AS</given-names></name><name><surname>Kline</surname><given-names>DG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Brachial plexus injury: a survey of 100 consecutive cases from a single service</article-title><source>Neurosurgery</source><year>2002</year><volume>51</volume><fpage>673</fpage><lpage>82</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12188945</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00006123-200209000-00011</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group